    "key": "ducts.apply",
    "displayName": "Apply Duct Losses",
    "intent": "Mutate",
    "costTier": "Mutation",
    "visibility": "EscalationVisible",
    "needs": "project-document",
    "description": "Write duct losses into Revit so they travel with the model. Each fitting names a method: pe-server points it at the Pe loss server, which charges the family's own coefficient parameter live (the fittingCoefficient slot, default Pe_C) when the family carries one and otherwise prices each leg live from the write's ASHRAE table and the connectors' flows (taps, transitions, unstamped elbows); specific-coefficient freezes a number (export only). Revit's own ASHRAE-table route is never written. Also Specific Loss (in-wg) on duct accessories, terminal connector drops where the family connector is Specific Loss, fan external static on equipment through the fanStatic slot, and Pe's provenance store in the hidden _PE_DuctLosses Project Information parameter. previewOnly plans every write and refusal without a transaction. A real apply commits Not Defined on every targeted fitting, then the losses, in one undo step; a failed stage rolls everything back and is named. Returns per-target outcomes and the touched systems' critical path after.",
