    "description": "Export native meshes and sized straight physical runs in host internal feet. focusOnly captures host elementIds without context. Context defaults to native boxes and sized runs without tessellating context; contextRepresentation meshes explicitly acquires Coarse context within contextPaddingFt of focus bounds, or explicit bounds. none suppresses context. Primitive rows own zero vertices; representation distinguishes mesh, box and run. Metadata phase distinguishes focus/context, unavailableElements identifies requested ids without meshes, omittedElements counts context excluded by the output budget, and completeness reports deferred context and acquisition resource limits. Successful artifacts preserve focus membership; unsupported parametric focus retains Medium/Fine meshes. Native triangle counts stop further acquisition after each tessellated face, so one already allocated face can exceed the acquisition budget. Completeness discloses omitted or deferred context. No document mutation. Browser orbit, visibility and cuts need no further native calls.",
    "searchTerms": [
      "space",
      "3d",
      "mesh",
      "viewer",
      "context",
      "section"
    ],
